 "skill_friction": [
  "Step 5 says 'If you can write a recommendation for the question, you have a basis: do not ask', but the Undeliverable-responsibility special case says ask if it defeats the main purpose, and the delivery-channel fork (Campaign vs Data 360/Marketing Cloud) needs completely different components. Nearly every fork admits a recommendation, so the two rules conflict; I asked anyway because the channel fork would make the inventory substantially wrong, and the hidden intent (Marketing Cloud) confirmed my recommendation would have been wrong.",
